# SimpleOS production status ledger — canonical owner + maturity per subsystem.
# Master plan: doc/01_research/domain/simpleos_production_host_master_plan.md §22 Phase 0.
# Guarded by test/01_unit/os/arch/duplicate_owner_spec.spl (ledger/code parity).
# maturity: production | partial | model | evidence-only | host-proxy | stub | duplicate
# Progress notes reflect landed+pushed convergence tranches (2026-07-27):
#   Stage S/P/INT, T2 (container/DeviceGrant/flock), T3-T4 (Podman-MDSOC+ mgr+OCI),
#   FV/FV2 (Lean proofs), SVC (service_v1), UPD (TUF), SQ (SQLite-VFS contract).

production_status:
  abi_contract:
    owner: os.kernel.abi.abi_v1
    lane: A00
    maturity: partial
    note: ABI v1 frozen by reference (Stage S); duplicate-owner guard green
  kernel_types:
    owner: os.kernel.types
    lane: A00
    maturity: production
  ipc:
    owner: os.kernel.ipc
    lane: A01
    maturity: partial
    note: single-use capability guard landed + Lean-proven (SingleUse); l4_fast_ipc marked honest model; reply object landed as MODEL only (reply_object.spl — one-shot reply cap reusing SingleUseLedger, call/notify distinction, caller-death invalidation, atomic deny-wins handle transfer via spawn_with_cspace_tracked; spec reply_object_spec.spl); NOT wired to syscall_ipc and NOT on any boot path; full endpoint/reply/notification fastpath + two-process QEMU call/reply evidence still OUTSTANDING (gate in .spipe/ipc_reply_object/state.md)
  capability_spawn:
    owner: os.kernel.ipc.cspace_spawn
    lane: A02
    maturity: model
    note: root-only ambient-spawn guard wired (3/3 sites); SpawnSpec MIGRATION LANDED — spawn_recipes.spl declares least-authority (READ|EXEC only, narrow path prefix) recipes for the 3 real userland spawn callers (shell exec.spl, riscv32/64 console launch, launcher_registry app launch) and all 3 syscall_process gates + the fs-exec bridge now mint through spawn_with_cspace instead of spawn_full when a recipe is declared; WM confirmed NOT a spawn caller (ECS entity spawn only), sshd out of lane scope; boot seal STILL GATED OFF (_seal_ambient_spawn_on_boot -> false, init_services.spl untouched); REMAINING TO ARM = (1) wire spawn_recipe_seed_parent_caps into boot — an ambient full() parent holds ZERO concrete tokens so cspace_spawn._find_source rejects every recipe grant and mints deny-all without it, (2) the one-line flag flip, (3) real-firmware QEMU boot+launch transcript showing a post-seal recipe spawn succeeding and an unmigrated ambient spawn denied; sealed-behaviour proof (no flag flip) = test/01_unit/os/kernel/loader/spawn_seal_readiness_spec.spl; resume plan .spipe/boot_seal_prep/state.md; live child CSpace injection + ring-3 recipe syscall argument still pending; P8xP2 profile meet-point landed (spawn_effective_rights_with_profile, contract spec 16 examples 0 failures)
  loader:
    owner: os.kernel.loader
    lane: A02
    maturity: partial
    note: spawn_authority guard + effective-rights helpers landed; descriptor-based exec pending
  memory:
    owner: os.kernel.memory
    lane: A02
    maturity: partial
  vfs:
    owner: os.kernel.fs
    lane: A03
    maturity: partial
    note: VfsHandleTable handle->mount routing landed (8 mounts[0] bypasses removed in services/vfs + LLM dispatch); src/lib fs_driver + 4 FAT32 copies still coexist — full collapse multi-increment; FAT32 copies 4->3, deleted src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/fs_driver/fat32_{core,dir_ops,hardening,parsers,stub,test_device}.spl (3165 lines, shadowed dead code: std.fs_driver.* resolves nogc_async_mut first, zero explicit importers; proven by async-only-symbol probe + failing sync-path control). FAT32B increment: sync fs_driver tier collapsed to shims — deleted ramfs/mount_table/direct_io/extension/driver_adapter/instance/ops (2477 lines, same shadowing, 15-vs-15 lockstep commit history, zero explicit importers) + orphaned fat32_cache.spl and its 2 spec copies (1017 lines; VFS2 delete-condition resolved: async fat32_core has 0 Dict refs / 77 flat-cache-field refs, never adopted it, and doc/09_report/nogc_eviction_leak_audit_2026-07-25.md confirms a leak in its 4 classes). −3494 net; 25 stale @cover paths repointed to async + 1 VFS2 dangling read_file guard repaired; all spec block counts byte-identical to baseline, Stage-S duplicate_owner guard 7 ✓/0 ✗, resolve probe PASS on JIT and interpreter. FAT32C increment: retired legacy driver deleted — src/os/services/fat32/{fat32,fat32_write,fat32_filesystem_ops,fat32_write_helpers}.spl (2122 lines) plus its 2 orphaned fat32_spec.spl copies (106 lines); island re-verified independently (zero src/ importers, imported only by each other, shared_fat32_driver delegates to std.fs_driver.fat32_core, no boot path / image builder / .shs reference). vfs_pure_fat_production_guard_spec.spl guard block was NOT removed but STRENGTHENED from non-use to absence: _assert_legacy_fat_implementation_files_deleted() asserts the 4 paths never reappear under src/os, and the tree walk lost its 4-file exemption so it now covers all of src/os; negative control confirmed the new assertion fails when the files are present (JIT + interpreter). −2232 net (git diff --stat: 22 insertions / 2254 deletions). All 15 vfs/arch/fs_driver spec block counts byte-identical to baseline; Stage-S duplicate_owner guard 7 ✓/0 ✗ on JIT and interpreter. FAT32 copies 3->2 — remaining: src/os/kernel/fs/fat32.spl (813, blocked on a target_presets.spl allowed_families decision, boot-path change needing QEMU+board validation); plan in .spipe/fs_stack_collapse/state.md §6 and .spipe/fat32_island_deletion/state.md
  drivers:
    owner: os.drivers
    lane: A04
    maturity: partial
    note: DeviceGrant runtime ABI + 10-step crash-revocation ordering landed + Lean-proven (no-DMA-without-IOMMU); wiring into real driver bind/crash path pending
  posix:
    owner: os.posix
    lane: A05
    maturity: partial
    note: writable shared mmap now has a kernel MODEL (vmm_shared.spl shared page-cache objects + rights attenuation + msync/last-unmap write-back; spec 7 blocks/35 examples/0 failures on JIT and interpreter); physical-frame path unproven (needs OVMF QEMU two-task gate), libc mmap still fails closed EOPNOTSUPP, syscall/VFS wiring not landed, SQLite WAL still blocked; no pthreads
  tty:
    owner: os.kernel tty paths
    lane: A06
    maturity: partial
    note: tty_write now delivers bytes to a drainable output buffer; PTY master/slave round-trip pending
  ssh:
    owner: os simple-native sshd
    lane: A06
    maturity: model
    note: maturity=model UNDERSTATES this - recommend partial. OpenSSH port RETRACTED as the production path - pure-Simple server src/os/apps/sshd (9576 lines) implements transport+curve25519 KEX+strict-kex+ext-info, ed25519/rsa-sha2-256,512/ecdsa-p256 host keys, aes256/128-gcm + aes256-ctr-etm (note: the LIVE server path ssh_cipher_live.spl is C-accelerated via tls13_aes256_gcm_helper.c; the pure-Simple ssh_cipher.spl is what the client uses), hmac-sha2-etm, channels/pty/exec, and interops with a real OpenSSH client in the x64 QEMU gate; pure-Simple client src/os/tools/net/_SshTool (1045 lines) reuses that core. rt_ssh_* SFFI (ssh_sffi/ssh_ffi) is a dead facade - NOP/weak-nil stubs only, no libssh2 anywhere. GAPS: ssh_kex.spl does not re-export ssh_sign_exchange_hash so ssh_kex_hostkey_matrix_spec is 1/7 (6x 'function not found', its rsa/ecdsa/kexinit describes never run) and ssh_kex_rsa_contract_spec is 0/1 - the whole host-key signing matrix is UNVERIFIED at HEAD on BOTH engines (one-line export fix); publickey userauth signature verify DISABLED (ssh_auth.spl:354), plaintext password store, no server-initiated rekey threshold (client-initiated rekey works), no subsystem/sftp, no port-forward, no chacha20-poly1305, client not wired to guest shell (register_tools.spl:91 stub) and blocked on guest rt_io_tcp_connect being a NOP. Bounded day-scale work, not multi-week. Survey: .spipe/ssh_native_survey/state.md
  containers:
    owner: os container contract
    lane: A07
    maturity: partial
    note: kernel ContainerNamespaceView rootless deny-by-default enforcement + Lean-proven isolation; Podman-on-MDSOC+ manager (sys_create/pod_wire/start/stop) + OCI edge adapter landed. ENFORCED LIVE (one lookup family only) — VfsManager path ops (open/stat/readdir/mkdir/rmdir/unlink/rename/symlink/read/preload/write) now converge on enforce_lookup_grants(), which is deny-wins over the ai-cli grant AND container_view_allows_path from the kernel primitive (no second enforcement path); host context (container_view nil) short-circuits to allow, so non-container callers are byte-identical to before; a rootless/stopped container's view resolves nothing (sys_stop and the reaper already reset the view to container_view_rootless). Spec container_lookup_enforcement_spec.spl 13/13 on JIT and interpreter, 2 deliberate-red calibrations (namespace gate off -> 10 red; rootless fail-open -> exactly the 2 fail-closed rows red). STILL MODEL-ONLY: nothing binds a running task to a VfsManager view (no caller of enter_container_view outside the spec — needs a per-container VfsManager or a task-local view slot), pid lookup (pt_ext_lookup / schedctl_op_get_*) is entirely ungated, the g_vfs_* free functions in vfs_write_ops.spl bypass VfsManager and are unenforced, and nothing is armed on a boot path; QEMU/boot evidence still blocked. Plan in .spipe/container_live_wiring/state.md
  web_server:
    owner: os.http
    lane: A09
    maturity: partial
    note: native raw benchmark fast; routed server interpreter-bound
  database:
    owner: simple db embedded (SDN store)
    lane: A09
    maturity: partial
    note: SQLite sqlite3_vfs contract landed (rollback-journal supported, WAL honestly gated on absent shared mmap); actual SQLite amalgamation build is multi-session (C toolchain blocked); server tier increment 1 (sessions, capabilities, per-session write overlay, read-committed isolation) + increment 2 DURABILITY landed at src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/database/server/ — COMMIT now persists through SdnDatabase.save() (FileLock + temp + fsync + rename) BEFORE it acknowledges, all-or-nothing, crash-point matrix green at before/mid/after-persist and on a recoverable persist failure (16 examples, 3 mutants killed 12/2/1); still MODEL-ONLY: no listener (serve() drains an in-memory transport, no socket), no concurrency primitive, OPEN still trusts the claimed principal, single-row GET/PUT/DEL only, read-committed not snapshot isolation, SdnRow._version is not serialized so the optimistic check resets across a restart, and a crash after persist before ack makes the tier at-least-once (no commit ids)
  config:
    owner: std.config (to extract from IDE config)
    lane: A10
    maturity: partial
    note: std.config core extracted to src/lib/common/config_core (schema+layers, mandatory-as-ceiling); IDE call-site swap pending; second non-IDE consumer = std.test_runner.test_config (TestConfig schema + workspace/session/mandatory layers, hand-rolled merge deleted)
  browser:
    owner: browser tree
    lane: A10
    maturity: model
    note: production-blocking isolation/origin/lifecycle gaps (renderer/network/GPU split multi-session)
  llm_profiles:
    owner: os security llm profile registry
    lane: A07
    maturity: partial
    note: profile registry (deny-wins intersection, 6 built-ins) + spawn effective-rights adapter landed + Lean-proven attenuation; live spawn-syscall wiring pending; P8xP2 meet-point landed (adapter routes through spawn_authority.spawn_effective_rights_with_profile)
  service_manifest:
    owner: os.services.service_manifest
    lane: A06
    maturity: partial
    note: typed service_v1 lifecycle/health/watchdog/restart-limit + §21 restart-drops-stale-grants invariant; 2 real services declaring — container_manager (restart drops manifest grants + brokered-out container pouches/views), tty_service (restart drops device grants + per-TTY pending-signal targeting); proven by test/01_unit/os/services/service_manifest_integration_spec.spl (9 blocks, 16 examples, 0 failures)
  update_tuf:
    owner: os.services.update.tuf_metadata
    lane: A07
    maturity: model
    note: TUF 4-role verifier (rollback/freeze/threshold/snapshot/untrusted-key defenses) PLUS real Ed25519 signature verification in os.services.update.tuf_signing — the "blocked on crypto stack" note was stale; Ed25519 re-verified byte-exact against RFC 8032 §7.1 T1/T3 (pubkey derivation + signature bytes) on BOTH JIT and interpreter via build/crypto2_kat/ed25519_kat_probe.spl, 9/9 checks; signatures cover an explicit length-prefixed canonical payload ("TUF1" domain tag, signatures_present excluded, targets use "TUFT"); untrusted/unkeyed signers rejected before any crypto, threshold counts DISTINCT cryptographically-verified signers, verification failure fails closed (TUF_BAD_SIGNATURE), rollback/freeze/snapshot checks unchanged; target artifacts digest-verified with real SHA-256; end-to-end proven by build/crypto2_kat/timing_probe.spl (valid update accepted code=0; one tampered signed byte rejected code=6); CAVEAT — the sspec tuf_signing_spec cannot be run under the shared test daemon (its 60s session-startup cap is exhausted by spec compile alone, yielding "no examples executed"); Ed25519 also forces interpreter fallback (JIT: "HIR lowering error: Unknown type: u128"), ~2.8s/op; A/B transactional install + SLSA provenance emission still pending
  formal_verification:
    owner: src.verification (kernel_capabilities + os_enforcement)
    lane: A11
    maturity: partial
    note: sorry-free Lean proofs — single-use, container isolation, device-grant no-DMA-without-IOMMU, profile attenuation; VFS-transaction/WAL-ordering invariants pending
  evidence:
    owner: spipe sdn receipts
    lane: A11
    maturity: partial
    note: fail-closed on missing/stale artifacts not yet universal; first two consumers wired (duplicate_owner_spec ledger receipt + P6 lld_gate_receipt_spec blocked-artifact FAIL)
